mixin ButtonComponent-Abstract

  p.Article-Paragraph.
    The button has the reputation of the primitive #[+Term--YDID GUI component] from which the learning of
      #[+Term--YDID UI/UX frameworks] usually beings.
    However in spite of unremarkable appearance of rectangle with label, this component is #[+Keyword--YDID very]
      #[+Keyword__Contrast--YDID deceptive] with its #[+Keyword--YDID apparent] simplicity.

  p.Article-Paragraph.
    The appearance of button could have #[+ImportantEntity--YDID 3] #[+Term--YDID HTML elements]:
      #[+ImportantEntity__Code--YDID button], #[+ImportantEntity__Code--YDID input] and #[+ImportantEntity__Code--YDID a],
      herewith, each one have own features.
    However, #[+Keyword--YDID only] #[+ImportantEntity__Code--YDID button] #[+Keyword--YDID and]
      #[+ImportantEntity__Code--YDID a] could have the child content, but #[+Keyword--YDID only]
      #[+ImportantEntity__Code--YDID button]　#[+Keyword--YDID and]　#[+ImportantEntity__Code--YDID input] could have
      #[+ImportantEntity__Code--YDID disabled] #[+Term--YDID attribute].

  p.Article-Paragraph.
    What about the #[+Term--YDID styles]?
    Well, the changing of border color or background color is very simple, but as the requirements gets closer to the
      today market's leve, the quantity of variables in equation increases sharply.
    Firs, being the control element, the button has the plenty of states such as #[+ImportantEntity__Code--YDID hover],
      #[+ImportantEntity__Code--YDID focus], #[+ImportantEntity__Code--YDID active],
      #[+ImportantEntity__Code--YDID disabled].
    All of these states must be visually distinguishable, herewith #[+Keyword--YDID for each] #[+Term--YDID theme]
      if any (it even does not&nbsp; matter the #[+Term--YDID theme] in #[+ImportantEntity--YDID YDF] understanding or no).
    Some of these states are mutually exclusive, some of these states could occur simultaneously thus the
    #[+Term--YDID styles] must be applied in certain order avoiding the conflicts.

  p.Article-Paragraph.
    And, what it the label does&nbsp;not fit in the button?
    What if required to add the SVG icon to button?
    All icons hase different sizes, and internal indents in SVG canvas is also different!
    The method of color changing in icon depends on it #[+Term--YDID SVG code], while icon must change its color depends
      on specific states of button!
    What is the button must have the square shape when it have only icon without label?
    (Although we are basically&nbsp;not recommend the icons without labels because their meaning could be
      not&nbsp;understood by the users with poor experience, the attempts to assure the customers avoid the using of
      icon-only button is not&nbsp;always successful).
    As far as respect these "what it"s, the output #[+Term--YDID CSS-code] becomes more complicated and large in volume.

  p.Article-Paragraph.
    From our side, we made all possible to encapsulate this complexity to clear API.
    Nevertheless, creating the valid #[+Term--YDID HTML] with respecting of #[+Term--YDID accessibility] and, if required,
      the #[+Term--YDID SEO], it is required to understand which #[+Term--YDID HTML code] will be generated.
